1
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,920
Have you slept enough?

2
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,319
Time to get up.

3
00:01:58,079 --> 00:01:59,319
The doctor said

4
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,560
we should talk to you more.

5
00:02:03,799 --> 00:02:04,599
He said you

6
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,159
can still hear us.

7
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,479
To be honest,

8
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:11,080
part of me

9
00:02:12,639 --> 00:02:14,759
really wishes you couldn't.

10
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:17,919
Just sleeping peacefully like this...

11
00:02:18,039 --> 00:02:18,599
how nice is that?

12
00:02:19,759 --> 00:02:21,039
Forget the crew,

13
00:02:22,199 --> 00:02:22,919
the money,

14
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:24,199
and the kids.

15
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,159
Leave it all behind.

16
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,800
You people are rotten to the core!

17
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:33,599
Messing with my uncle,

18
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,080
making a scene at Jinli Palace.

19
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:35,800
Now messing with me,

20
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,759
pulling the same old trick!

21
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,599
She's only 19!

22
00:02:38,879 --> 00:02:40,879
A grown man and a mother,

23
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,360
using a young girl against me!

24
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,719
Have you no shame?

25
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,879
Supervisor Guo, you've got it wrong.

26
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:47,599
We really had no other choice,

27
00:02:47,599 --> 00:02:48,639
that's why we came to you.

28
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:50,039
You know what your uncle is like.

29
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:50,800
You know him,

30
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:51,520
don't you?

31
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,719
Ask around the construction site.

32
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,960
Drinking, gambling, whoring, and extortion.

33
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,919
All his dealings with the Sai family...

34
00:02:58,280 --> 00:02:59,680
we have clear records of everything.

35
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,000
We have witnesses and physical evidence.

36
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,080
It's not just about Jinli Palace.

37
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,919
It's way more serious than that.

38
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,560
Lady, you're a real Saint!

39
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,599
I'm begging you.

40
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:06,560
If you have evidence,

41
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,719
bring it out and give it to the police!

42
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,199
Hurry up and get my uncle locked up,

43
00:03:09,319 --> 00:03:10,759
so I can finally get some peace and quiet!

44
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,319
Okay?

45
00:03:11,879 --> 00:03:12,919
You people are quite resourceful.

46
00:03:13,039 --> 00:03:14,319
You dug up that I'm his nephew.

47
00:03:14,759 --> 00:03:15,960
Did you also find out

48
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:18,360
that he's a gambling addict drowning in debt?

49
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:19,639
His wife ran off.

50
00:03:20,039 --> 00:03:20,840
My sister was only six.

51
00:03:21,479 --> 00:03:22,960
In the dead of winter, my mom

52
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,360
worked odd jobs to support me and my sister,

53
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,639
paying off his debts for 13 years!

54
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,560
For 13 whole years!

55
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,439
My mom said he was her brother,

56
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:32,960
he was family,

57
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:34,360
and we couldn't just abandon him.

58
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,000
As soon as one debt was paid, a new one came.

59
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,800
It never ended!

60
00:03:37,599 --> 00:03:39,199
You think I wanted to be a supervisor?

61
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,759
I have a civil engineering degree.

62
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,120
I was sitting in the AC at headquarters,

63
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,800
making 8,000 yuan a month!

64
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,599
Then my uncle got detained,

65
00:03:49,159 --> 00:03:50,439
fined for breach of contract,

66
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,120
and I took the heat.

67
00:03:52,719 --> 00:03:54,639
I was sent down here to cover for him!

68
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,960
Over 20 years ago,

69
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,680
you, me, and Old Wei...

70
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,439
the three of us...

71
00:04:06,719 --> 00:04:08,800
were drinking in our little yard.

72
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:12,439
We agreed to team up,

73
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:14,360
make big money,

74
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,599
live in new houses,

75
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:17,600
and become city folk.

76
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,600
And you really didn't forget.

77
00:04:21,439 --> 00:04:22,759
Even your bankbook's

78
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:24,839
PIN is that very date.

79
00:04:27,319 --> 00:04:28,720
All these years...

80
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:31,279
all the hardships we went through...

81
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,279
if you told people today,

82
00:04:33,279 --> 00:04:34,399
they wouldn't even believe it.

83
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:38,199
We're finally about to become city folk.

84
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:40,319
But look at you...

85
00:04:41,959 --> 00:04:43,360
Why are you lying down again?

86
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:50,279
Look at this.

87
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:52,240
Cancer.

88
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:55,040
With a question mark.

89
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,720
They're not even sure themselves.

90
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,480
A question mark...

91
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,319
Are they asking me?

92
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,040
Well, I don't accept this!

93
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,759
I feel like I'm still young.

94
00:05:13,199 --> 00:05:14,720
I can work for another 20 years!

95
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,920
Isn't this just sentencing me to death?

96
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,759
I can't accept this!

97
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:31,079
If you just lie here,

98
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,439
the family falls apart.

99
00:05:35,439 --> 00:05:36,319
What about me?

100
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,160
If I collapse too,

101
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,439
will this family

102
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:42,800
even hold together?

103
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,399
Both brothers married such overbearing wives,

104
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,240
and the third one's nothing but trouble.

105
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,480
If they start fighting over splitting the estate,

106
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,480
what are we going to do?

107
00:05:56,639 --> 00:05:57,600
While we're still alive,

108
00:05:58,639 --> 00:05:59,879
we can't leave any regrets.

109
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,519
Dacheng!

110
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,480
You're awake!

111
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:10,720
Doctor!

112
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,279
Doctor, he's awake!

113
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:13,519
Dacheng!

114
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,439
Thank goodness!

115
00:06:14,639 --> 00:06:15,680
I'll go get the doctor.

116
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,160
I was supposed to get married.

117
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:22,879
My uncle said he had connections

118
00:06:23,279 --> 00:06:24,279
and could plan the wedding for me.

119
00:06:25,279 --> 00:06:26,480
He took the money from my mom

120
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,639
and gambled it all away.

121
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,639
Now there isn't a penny left.

122
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,519
He's sitting in jail,

123
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:33,879
without a care in the world,

124
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,319
while I can't even afford

125
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,399
to buy my fiancee a wedding dress.

126
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:41,199
In a fit of rage, she said

127
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,120
the wedding is off.

128
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,240
I can make wedding dresses

129
00:07:28,759 --> 00:07:29,639
I'll burn some more money for you.

130
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:31,879
Just let me know if you need anything.

131
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,560
I guess you don't miss me either.

132
00:07:34,519 --> 00:07:35,879
Haven't seen you in my dreams for over a year.

133
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,120
Baolan.

134
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:39,879
Our first two...

135
00:07:41,199 --> 00:07:42,160
I've raised them all up.

136
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:45,439
Guihua.

137
00:07:46,079 --> 00:07:46,600
Take a look.

138
00:07:47,439 --> 00:07:49,439
The third and fourth are all grown up now.

139
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,240
My job here...

140
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:52,720
is pretty much done.

141
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,079
I've done right by both of you.

142
00:07:56,759 --> 00:07:57,319
Don't worry.

143
00:07:58,399 --> 00:07:59,839
You both gave your lives to me.

144
00:08:00,879 --> 00:08:02,040
No matter whose child it is,

145
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,240
I won't mistreat them.

146
00:08:06,439 --> 00:08:06,759
Dad.

147
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,519
The paper's almost finished burning.

148
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:09,959
Everything's wiped clean, too.

149
00:08:10,399 --> 00:08:11,160
Shouldn't we be heading back?

150
00:08:12,319 --> 00:08:12,639
Let's go.

151
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,480
Go on, go on.

152
00:08:15,759 --> 00:08:16,000
Let's go.

153
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,720
We'll visit you next year.

154
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,120
You go ahead. Go on first.

155
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,199
We're leaving, Stepmom.

156
00:08:22,639 --> 00:08:22,959
We're off.

157
00:08:32,399 --> 00:08:33,000
Oh, Baolan...

158
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:35,320
Our second boy has really made something of himself.

159
00:08:35,879 --> 00:08:37,000
Financially,

160
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,320
he has fewer burdens.

161
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,440
These old bones of mine...

162
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:44,039
I'm counting on him to bury me.

163
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,320
This family...

164
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:49,200
I plan to leave in his hands, too.

165
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:52,759
The oldest is watching over the construction crew,

166
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,399
and the second has an education,

167
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:57,360
so I'll have him handle the accounts.

168
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:00,120
As long as the brothers stay united,

169
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,519
this family won't fall apart.

170
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:04,960
Whoever is more capable

171
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,879
has to swallow more grievances.

172
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,039
Don't hold that against me.

173
00:09:13,559 --> 00:09:13,919
Time to go.

174
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,480
I'll visit you again another day.

175
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,039
Why did your dad suddenly invite us to dinner?

176
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:41,799
Dad, why are you...

177
00:09:41,799 --> 00:09:42,159
Xiuliang!

178
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,080
Why aren't you waiting inside?

179
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,559
Why stand out here?

180
00:09:43,679 --> 00:09:44,720
I was waiting for you!

181
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,320
Come here, come on.

182
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:46,720
Check out this car. Just bought it.

183
00:09:47,919 --> 00:09:48,600
Take a look. What do you think?

184
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,440
Isn't it sharp?

185
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,320
This is nice!

186
00:09:51,759 --> 00:09:53,080
Leather seats and all.

187
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,159
Genuine leather, every bit of it.

188
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,879
It sure is spacious.

189
00:09:57,879 --> 00:09:59,240
Your old pickup truck...

190
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:00,919
...was getting pretty beat-up.

191
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:01,960
Not great for doing business.

192
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,799
Replacing it makes total sense.

193
00:10:02,919 --> 00:10:04,120
Who said anything about replacing it?

194
00:10:04,279 --> 00:10:05,399
I bought this for you.

195
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:07,840
Take a look.

196
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:08,399
Isn't it great?

197
00:10:08,679 --> 00:10:09,840
Wait, Dad, Dad, Dad...

198
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:10,200
Hold on a second.

199
00:10:10,399 --> 00:10:11,360
Both of us already have cars.

200
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,399
Two cars are plenty for us.

201
00:10:12,679 --> 00:10:14,240
Your car's due for an upgrade anyway.

202
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:14,919
Besides...

203
00:10:15,159 --> 00:10:16,399
...with the demolition payout...

204
00:10:16,399 --> 00:10:18,200
...you did so much for our family.

205
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,200
Driving this car...

206
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,559
...and commuting with Meifan...

207
00:10:20,919 --> 00:10:21,559
...how sharp is that?

208
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:22,679
Dad...

209
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:24,639
We appreciate the thought,

210
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,279
but this car is just too expensive.

211
00:10:26,279 --> 00:10:26,919
Yeah, exactly, Dad.

212
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,080
There's really no need.

213
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,200
It's just family matters.

214
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,000
You don't need to do this...

215
00:10:30,039 --> 00:10:30,799
What do you mean, "no need"?

216
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:31,960
Sit inside and try it out.

217
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:32,759
Then you'll see if there's a need.

218
00:10:32,759 --> 00:10:33,799
I... I really don't...

219
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,480
We have cars. We don't need this.

220
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:36,639
You call that a car?

221
00:10:36,639 --> 00:10:37,440
That tiny little thing?

222
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,440
This is a seven-seater.

223
00:10:38,559 --> 00:10:39,799
It's huge and spacious!

224
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:40,799
There are only two of us in our home.

225
00:10:40,799 --> 00:10:41,679
What would I do with a seven-seater?

226
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:42,360
What do you mean, two?

227
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:44,679
Aren't you going to have kids later?

228
00:10:45,039 --> 00:10:46,679
Besides, look how many of us there are.

229
00:10:46,799 --> 00:10:48,360
From your big brother and his wife down to the fifth,

230
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,200
that's over ten of us!

231
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,600
This car won't even fit everyone!

232
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,720
Dad, if you want me to be a bus driver,

233
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,440
just say so.

234
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,240
What bus driver?

235
00:10:57,159 --> 00:10:59,240
Dad, Xiuliang didn't mean it like that.

236
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,440
Why don't we go inside first

237
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,159
and chat over dinner?

238
00:11:04,039 --> 00:11:04,919
All right, let's head in first.

239
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,440
Now that we got the demolition money,

240
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:17,879
the family

241
00:11:18,639 --> 00:11:19,720
has some extra cash.

242
00:11:21,279 --> 00:11:22,879
I didn't know how else to help you kids,

243
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,559
so I bought a car.

244
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,399
Who knew

245
00:11:26,679 --> 00:11:27,919
you wouldn't even want it.

246
00:11:29,639 --> 00:11:29,919
Dad,

247
00:11:30,919 --> 00:11:32,720
it's just that the car is too expensive.

248
00:11:33,519 --> 00:11:34,440
Besides, Xiuliang

249
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,000
helping out the family

250
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:36,840
is only natural.

251
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:37,960
Right, Xiuliang?

252
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,320
Dad, about the car,

253
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:40,840
let's put that aside for now.

254
00:11:41,759 --> 00:11:42,480
You called us here today,

255
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,360
did you have something else to discuss?

256
00:11:48,799 --> 00:11:51,440
Isn't the village being demolished?

257
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,159
Our housing situation is bound to change.

258
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,519
I just wanted to share my thoughts

259
00:11:56,919 --> 00:11:57,799
with you

260
00:11:57,799 --> 00:11:58,759
and talk it over.

261
00:11:58,879 --> 00:11:59,559
No need to discuss it.

262
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,039
You make the call.

263
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,120
We'll definitely agree with whatever you decide.

264
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:03,840
We're all for it.

265
00:12:04,399 --> 00:12:04,759
Right?

266
00:12:07,759 --> 00:12:08,919
What I'm thinking is,

267
00:12:09,799 --> 00:12:12,279
for the oldest's family and the third,

268
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,720
to buy a place for each of them.

269
00:12:14,519 --> 00:12:15,759
As for the oldest's place,

270
00:12:16,159 --> 00:12:17,879
it should be close to Zhenzhu's school,

271
00:12:18,519 --> 00:12:19,039
and a bit bigger,

272
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:20,559
so Xiaowu can live there too.

273
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,240
As for the third's place,

274
00:12:22,559 --> 00:12:23,360
well,

275
00:12:23,559 --> 00:12:24,360
in a better location,

276
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,360
so he can use it when he gets married.

277
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,720
Your Uncle Wei recommended

278
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,159
places at Huatai Mansion.

279
00:12:30,399 --> 00:12:31,600
I checked them out, and they're really nice.

280
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:32,759
Plus,

281
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,480
it's really close to the Port Authority.

282
00:12:36,039 --> 00:12:37,360
Just a ten-minute walk away.

283
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,639
And there's a hospital nearby,

284
00:12:39,799 --> 00:12:41,960
parks, schools, kindergartens...

285
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:42,639
It has everything.

286
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,440
It's just too big.

287
00:12:44,759 --> 00:12:46,399
The sales agent said

288
00:12:46,519 --> 00:12:49,399
it's suitable for two generations living together.

289
00:13:01,879 --> 00:13:03,399
I was thinking...

290
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,720
You two have been married all these years,

291
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,919
and still don't have kids.

292
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,840
Living in such a big place all by myself,

293
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,399
there's really no point.

294
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,240
If...

295
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,159
if we lived together,

296
00:13:17,759 --> 00:13:19,159
we could look out for each other.

297
00:13:20,279 --> 00:13:22,240
And if you ever have a baby down the road,

298
00:13:22,399 --> 00:13:24,200
I could lend a hand, couldn't I?

299
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:30,039
Dad, this whole thing...

300
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:32,799
it's just so sudden.

301
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,120
Sure, we're family,

302
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,360
but we have completely different habits.

303
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:37,720
Right?

304
00:13:38,039 --> 00:13:38,919
If we live together,

305
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:40,360
we're bound to bump heads sooner or later.

306
00:13:40,519 --> 00:13:41,720
There's really no need.

307
00:13:41,759 --> 00:13:42,320
When that happens,

308
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,120
you'll just feel upset and suffocated.

309
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:44,919
Yeah, and we'd feel awkward too.

310
00:13:44,919 --> 00:13:45,600
That's right, Dad.

311
00:13:45,919 --> 00:13:47,440
Mostly, it's that we're younger,

312
00:13:47,559 --> 00:13:48,600
and our daily schedule is pretty erratic.

313
00:13:48,759 --> 00:13:49,600
We'd hate to disturb your rest.

314
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,080
Exactly.

315
00:13:50,159 --> 00:13:51,159
With Meifan's line of work,

316
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,200
her hours can be really irregular.

317
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,799
You love getting up early for walks,

318
00:13:53,879 --> 00:13:55,080
while we love sleeping in.

319
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,559
And you love watching Chinese opera,

320
00:13:56,559 --> 00:13:57,639
while we prefer watching the news.

321
00:13:57,919 --> 00:13:58,480
Not to mention our meals.

322
00:13:58,480 --> 00:13:59,440
You like heavy, salty flavors,

323
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,240
while we prefer to eat light.

324
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:00,759
I... I...

325
00:14:00,759 --> 00:14:02,000
Those are all minor things.

326
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,440
We can always work them out.

327
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:03,960
Right, of course,

328
00:14:04,159 --> 00:14:04,840
they are minor things.

329
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,320
Even so...

330
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,080
Even minor things

331
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,720
can lead to unnecessary friction.

332
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:08,519
Why put ourselves through that?

333
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:11,120
Besides, we're all adults now.

334
00:14:11,679 --> 00:14:13,000
We need a little privacy and personal space.

335
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,759
Keeping some distance between us,

336
00:14:15,279 --> 00:14:16,360
isn't that for the best?

337
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,159
Why do we have to squeeze in together?

338
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,320
So you just think I'm in your way.

339
00:14:19,639 --> 00:14:20,960
That's not what I meant.

340
00:14:21,639 --> 00:14:21,960
I mean...

341
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:24,519
Meifan,

342
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,519
what do you think?

343
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,240
Dad,

344
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:33,600
has something been bothering you lately?

345
00:14:33,919 --> 00:14:35,000
Just talk to us.

346
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:36,759
If we can help, we definitely will.

347
00:14:43,039 --> 00:14:43,879
Let me ask you this.

348
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,440
If your own in-laws

349
00:14:47,639 --> 00:14:49,320
insisted on moving in with you,

350
00:14:49,559 --> 00:14:51,559
would you just brush them off

351
00:14:51,559 --> 00:14:52,399
by claiming it's inconvenient?

352
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,120
The two of them

353
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,919
would never even dream of doing that.

354
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:02,879
Dad,

355
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,960
we actually do have something to tell you today.

356
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,360
About Xiuliang's job...

357
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:07,759
Meifan!

358
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:12,320
Why don't you order first?

359
00:15:13,519 --> 00:15:14,519
We've been sitting here talking for ages.

360
00:15:19,639 --> 00:15:20,120
Hold on.

361
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:21,360
What did you just say?

362
00:15:21,799 --> 00:15:23,000
What's going on with Xiuliang's job?

363
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,200
Just... don't order anything too spicy.

364
00:15:24,559 --> 00:15:25,559
Dad can't handle spicy food.

365
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:26,720
It upsets his stomach.

366
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,799
Are you two hiding something from me?

367
00:15:35,159 --> 00:15:35,639
Well...

368
00:15:36,879 --> 00:15:37,720
Dad, lately...

369
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,000
he really has been...

370
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,600
under massive pressure at work.

371
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,399
He's up all night, unable to sleep.

372
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:45,679
Anyway...

373
00:15:45,679 --> 00:15:47,519
it's just stuff we shouldn't bother you with.

374
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,440
As for us,

375
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:50,240
even if we just lived close by,

376
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,799
just a quick walk over to your place,

377
00:15:51,799 --> 00:15:53,159
and came by to see you every day,

378
00:15:53,159 --> 00:15:53,759
that would work fine.

379
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,440
It's really no different from living together.

380
00:15:55,679 --> 00:15:56,799
"Shouldn't bother me," right?

381
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,320
Then don't tell me anything at all.

382
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,120
Today,

383
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:03,120
I'm just getting the cold shoulder!

384
00:16:03,279 --> 00:16:05,000
Don't you want your own lives?

385
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:05,559
Fine.

386
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,519
Then go live your lives on your own.

387
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:08,759
Fine!

388
00:16:40,679 --> 00:16:41,039
Come in.

389
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:42,960
Director Jin.

390
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,360
A colleague from the lab was just looking for you.

391
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,519
Said he called you, but you didn't answer.

392
00:16:47,279 --> 00:16:47,720
Who was it?

393
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:48,759
Dr. Cao Jian.

394
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:50,279
Thanks.

395
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:00,799
Old Cao.

396
00:17:00,919 --> 00:17:01,440
It's me.

397
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:03,840
I didn't hear my phone just now.

398
00:17:04,119 --> 00:17:04,480
What's up?

399
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:07,680
Yes.

400
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:09,759
My father-in-law's last name is Sai.

401
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:10,799
Sai Duoxi.

402
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:17,920
I'll be right over.

403
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:25,519
Dad.

404
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:26,960
You startled me.

405
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,079
What's with your eyes?

406
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:29,640
Are you nearsighted?

407
00:17:31,119 --> 00:17:31,839
They're just for show.

408
00:17:32,519 --> 00:17:33,119
Do they look good?

409
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,279
Good? Not at all.

410
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,079
Your eyes look fine on their own.

411
00:17:36,079 --> 00:17:37,319
Putting on these glasses...

412
00:17:37,319 --> 00:17:37,720
doesn't look good.

413
00:17:38,039 --> 00:17:39,640
It makes me look educated.

414
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:42,200
Educated? Does being educated come from glasses?

415
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:43,960
Take them off. They look bad.

416
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:46,079
Dad.

417
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:48,960
You don't look well.

418
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,519
A lot of work at the site lately?

419
00:17:53,559 --> 00:17:55,160
Lots of work. Busy.

420
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,000
Tired.

421
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,319
Just completely exhausted.

422
00:17:57,759 --> 00:17:58,480
I've realized...

423
00:17:58,799 --> 00:17:59,759
I don't come home enough.

424
00:17:59,759 --> 00:18:00,720
Neither of us feels right like this.

425
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:01,680
How about this?

426
00:18:02,119 --> 00:18:03,160
Once the village relocates,

427
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,720
come live with me.

428
00:18:05,519 --> 00:18:06,880
Stop talking nonsense.

429
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,759
You're already married.

430
00:18:09,319 --> 00:18:10,559
You can't just take your dad along with you.

431
00:18:11,759 --> 00:18:12,200
Dad...

432
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,359
Come on, don't joke around.

433
00:18:14,359 --> 00:18:15,359
Could you be mistaken?

434
00:18:15,559 --> 00:18:16,400
I'm not mistaken.

435
00:18:16,519 --> 00:18:17,559
Name, age...

436
00:18:17,839 --> 00:18:18,960
I've double-checked everything.

437
00:18:20,119 --> 00:18:22,000
The clinical features are completely textbook.

438
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,960
Wait, is your hospital competent enough?

439
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,839
Could it be a misdiagnosis?

440
00:18:27,039 --> 00:18:27,720
Xiuliang.

441
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,319
Combining the MRI with all clinical indicators,

442
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,519
the chance of a misdiagnosis is extremely slim.

443
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:34,359
Otherwise, the hospital wouldn't be rushing

444
00:18:34,359 --> 00:18:35,599
to have him undergo a needle biopsy.

445
00:18:35,799 --> 00:18:37,079
You have to trust me on this.

446
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:56,599
Is he okay?

447
00:19:00,079 --> 00:19:00,960
Does he know yet?

448
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,640
The test results...

449
00:19:03,039 --> 00:19:04,079
He picked them up himself.

450
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:08,440
About this...

451
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,160
who else knows right now?

452
00:19:15,359 --> 00:19:16,119
Other than you and me,

453
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:17,240
nobody knows.

454
00:19:18,799 --> 00:19:19,440
Listen to me.

455
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:21,920
You can't tell anyone.

456
00:19:23,119 --> 00:19:23,799
Why not?

457
00:19:23,799 --> 00:19:24,759
Think about the Ma family.

458
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,200
Think about what our family's dealing with.

459
00:19:28,519 --> 00:19:29,880
The old man is deliberately hiding it from us.

460
00:19:30,359 --> 00:19:31,559
Fine, I understand, I get it.

461
00:19:32,559 --> 00:19:32,839
But...

462
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,559
money is one thing, and illness is another.

463
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,319
He's sick right now.

464
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,119
Are you just going to keep it quiet?

465
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:41,599
I think...

466
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,119
the old man isn't ready himself.

467
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:46,480
Until he tells the family,

468
00:19:47,599 --> 00:19:49,000
you and I both have to act like we don't know.

469
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,880
Jingran treats you well, too.

470
00:19:57,559 --> 00:19:59,039
Just settle down

471
00:19:59,599 --> 00:20:00,599
and live a good life with him.

472
00:20:01,119 --> 00:20:02,359
As long as you're safe and healthy,

473
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:03,839
Dad can rest easy.

474
00:20:04,279 --> 00:20:05,440
He is pretty good.

475
00:20:06,039 --> 00:20:07,079
Good-tempered,

476
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,359
and makes decent money.

477
00:20:08,359 --> 00:20:09,079
That's right.

478
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,359
Don't forget

479
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,519
who picked your husband for you.

480
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,680
How should I put it...

481
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:15,880
He's been acting weird lately.

482
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,039
He doesn't treat me as well as you do.

483
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:17,880
What's wrong?

484
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,319
Things aren't going well at his work.

485
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:22,559
His department head got promoted,

486
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,039
and isn't he the deputy head?

487
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,880
They say he has a shot at department head,

488
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:27,480
so that's all he thinks about.

489
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:29,839
Forget about him. Eat up, eat up.

490
00:20:30,799 --> 00:20:31,599
You eat too. Go on, eat.

491
00:20:31,799 --> 00:20:32,160
While it's hot.

492
00:20:33,279 --> 00:20:34,000
Lao Si...

493
00:20:34,519 --> 00:20:35,160
Remember this:

494
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:36,960
no matter what happens,

495
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:39,839
if you're having a hard time,

496
00:20:40,359 --> 00:20:41,119
come home to Dad.

497
00:21:56,039 --> 00:21:56,319
Dad.

498
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:13,960
I'm here to grab the car keys.

499
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:19,480
Aren't you worried people will think you're just a driver?

500
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:23,759
Uncle Wei said

501
00:22:24,279 --> 00:22:25,279
the units at Huatai Mansion,

502
00:22:26,759 --> 00:22:27,799
we should go check them out soon.

503
00:22:29,039 --> 00:22:29,839
After all, right now,

504
00:22:30,279 --> 00:22:31,400
house prices change by the day.

505
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:32,880
The sooner, the better.

506
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,440
I haven't made up my mind about buying yet.

507
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,480
It's too big.

508
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:42,599
If we're buying, let's get a big one.

509
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:44,559
A four-bedroom.

510
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:46,079
One room for you,

511
00:22:46,319 --> 00:22:47,599
one for us, one for Xiao Wu,

512
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,799
and for the remaining room, whoever stays,

513
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:50,640
there'll be plenty of space.

514
00:22:52,799 --> 00:22:53,880
Did your wife agree to this?

515
00:22:58,799 --> 00:22:59,640
We're all family.

516
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:00,799
Why wouldn't she?

517
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:09,960
Son,

518
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:13,960
keep an eye out

519
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:15,000
for other apartments too.

520
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,640
Look out for your eldest brother

521
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,000
and for the third one and the rest.

522
00:23:18,759 --> 00:23:19,240
This place

523
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:21,000
could be torn down at any moment.

524
00:23:23,039 --> 00:23:23,319
Got it.

525
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:49,480
Dad.

526
00:23:49,799 --> 00:23:50,319
Um,

527
00:23:50,519 --> 00:23:50,920
the keys...

528
00:23:53,359 --> 00:23:54,119
The car keys, Dad.

529
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,000
Well, I'll head back now, then.

530
00:24:10,759 --> 00:24:11,920
I'll come back for the holidays.

531
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:14,519
Go on back.

532
00:24:43,599 --> 00:24:44,000
Eldest!

533
00:24:45,279 --> 00:24:46,799
Come downstairs with Zhenzhu's mom.

534
00:24:46,839 --> 00:24:47,200
Coming!

535
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:53,559
Did you hear me?

536
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:54,720
Dad's calling us.

537
00:24:54,799 --> 00:24:55,359
He wants to talk.

538
00:24:55,519 --> 00:24:56,440
What's there to talk about?

539
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:59,000
We worked so hard to collect the phase two payment,

540
00:24:59,559 --> 00:25:00,319
and Dad just turns around...

541
00:25:00,799 --> 00:25:01,920
...and buys your brother a new car!

542
00:25:03,319 --> 00:25:04,039
Buys him a— Eldest!

543
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:06,240
Coming!

544
00:25:06,559 --> 00:25:07,240
Hurry it up.

545
00:25:07,519 --> 00:25:08,799
Maybe Dad'll buy you an apartment too!

546
00:25:11,599 --> 00:25:12,400
Come on, hurry up!

547
00:25:21,039 --> 00:25:21,400
Dad.

548
00:25:23,319 --> 00:25:24,000
Come on, come in.

549
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:25,440
Have a seat.

550
00:25:26,599 --> 00:25:26,880
Sit.

551
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:29,079
What did you

552
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:31,119
want to see us

553
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:32,279
about?

554
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:34,400
Here.

555
00:25:35,319 --> 00:25:35,720
Take it.

556
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:40,519
What's this...?

557
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:43,119
Didn't the project money come in?

558
00:25:43,799 --> 00:25:44,799
You've had it tough too.

559
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:45,559
Just take it.

560
00:25:50,519 --> 00:25:50,880
Dad,

561
00:25:51,279 --> 00:25:52,839
this is just what we're supposed to do.

562
00:25:53,640 --> 00:25:54,559
We can't take this money.

563
00:25:56,079 --> 00:25:56,519
No, really.

564
00:25:56,839 --> 00:25:57,680
Zhenzhu's mom,

565
00:25:58,319 --> 00:26:00,319
ever since your mother-in-law passed away,

566
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:02,160
this family...

567
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:04,279
you've really worked yourself to the bone.

568
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:05,599
And my eldest...

569
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:07,000
He dropped out of school

570
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,319
to work the construction sites with me.

571
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,400
He's had it so rough, too.

572
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:14,759
Deep down, I've always felt I let him down.

573
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:16,240
Now,

574
00:26:16,559 --> 00:26:18,720
our village is going to be demolished.

575
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:19,640
This house...

576
00:26:19,920 --> 00:26:21,200
will be torn down in no time.

577
00:26:21,559 --> 00:26:22,400
Down the road,

578
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:23,799
where we're all going to live...

579
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:27,119
I haven't talked to you about it yet.

580
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:29,400
Here's what I'm thinking.

581
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:32,160
Right by

582
00:26:33,119 --> 00:26:34,440
Honggang No. 2 Middle School,

583
00:26:35,519 --> 00:26:37,400
I'll buy you a three-bedroom apartment.

584
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:38,559
That way,

585
00:26:38,839 --> 00:26:40,200
for the three of you,

586
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,160
it'll be plenty of space.

587
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:41,839
And what's more,

588
00:26:42,359 --> 00:26:44,880
the tuition money Zhenzhu needs for school,

589
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:46,400
I've set that aside too.

590
00:26:47,039 --> 00:26:48,200
Don't worry about a thing.

591
00:26:49,599 --> 00:26:49,880
Dad,

592
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:51,240
are you...

593
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:54,000
not planning to live with us?

594
00:26:55,119 --> 00:26:55,920
Look,

595
00:26:56,119 --> 00:26:58,200
Zhenzhu is in seventh grade now.

596
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,240
If I move in,

597
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:01,599
and the others come visit,

598
00:27:01,839 --> 00:27:03,720
with the whole family trooping in and out,

599
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:05,480
Zhenzhu really needs

600
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:07,240
a quiet place to study.

601
00:27:07,359 --> 00:27:08,000
Besides,

602
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:10,079
ever since Zhenzhu's mom married into our family,

603
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:11,480
all these years,

604
00:27:11,559 --> 00:27:13,720
she's waited on over a dozen people.

605
00:27:14,279 --> 00:27:15,519
It's been so exhausting.

606
00:27:15,839 --> 00:27:17,200
She deserves a break.

607
00:27:17,559 --> 00:27:19,839
Dad, if you're not living with us,

608
00:27:19,839 --> 00:27:20,400
where... where are...

609
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:21,519
where will you live?

610
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,839
I'll just buy another place for myself.

611
00:27:26,839 --> 00:27:27,559
Live on my own.

612
00:27:27,759 --> 00:27:29,799
If my second son and the others want to visit,

613
00:27:29,799 --> 00:27:30,599
they can come stay.

614
00:27:31,119 --> 00:27:31,799
If they don't,

615
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,240
living alone suits me just fine.

616
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:34,920
First, you...

617
00:27:39,119 --> 00:27:39,799
Zhenzhu's mom, you...

618
00:27:40,079 --> 00:27:40,920
What's gotten into you?

619
00:27:41,599 --> 00:27:42,000
Dad,

620
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,319
did I do something wrong?

621
00:27:45,559 --> 00:27:46,880
If... If I did something wrong,

622
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,279
tell me and I'll fix it.

623
00:27:48,279 --> 00:27:48,680
No, not at all!

624
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:49,720
I'll definitely change.

625
00:27:50,079 --> 00:27:50,880
Dad, I know.

626
00:27:51,319 --> 00:27:52,680
Back when I married Xiuming,

627
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:53,519
you weren't happy about it.

628
00:27:53,519 --> 00:27:54,400
You weren't satisfied with me.

629
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:56,079
But what's done is done—I married him.

630
00:27:56,519 --> 00:27:58,640
I've been in this Sai family for nearly 20 years.

631
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,000
I respected my in-laws,

632
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,319
and looked after his siblings.

633
00:28:01,319 --> 00:28:03,720
I raised Xiao Wu with my own hands.

634
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,480
And Xiuhe and Qianjin's mother,

635
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,880
who was bedridden for all those years—

636
00:28:08,039 --> 00:28:09,359
I was the one who took care of her.

637
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:10,680
When she passed,

638
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:12,680
she was clean from head to toe.

639
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:14,240
The room didn't have the slightest smell.

640
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:16,440
She didn't even have a single bedsore.

641
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:18,400
Even if you don't credit my achievements,

642
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:19,680
you must acknowledge all my hard work!

643
00:28:20,039 --> 00:28:22,279
Why did I give so much to this family?

644
00:28:22,279 --> 00:28:22,920
Because...

645
00:28:23,319 --> 00:28:24,240
this family...

646
00:28:24,839 --> 00:28:26,400
I treated it as my very own.

647
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:28,160
I treated you like my own father.

648
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:28,920
I feel like...

649
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:29,480
I know...

650
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:30,319
all the effort I put in...

651
00:28:30,319 --> 00:28:32,079
It's all... it's all completely wasted!

652
00:28:32,079 --> 00:28:32,920
Zhenzhu's mom,

653
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,839
that's not what I meant!

654
00:28:34,839 --> 00:28:35,839
Come on, get up, quick—

655
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,839
I have four sons.

656
00:28:37,839 --> 00:28:40,480
I can't keep making the two of you suffer.

657
00:28:40,480 --> 00:28:42,079
I can't take advantage of honest people.

658
00:28:42,079 --> 00:28:44,240
When you decided to live with the second son,

659
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:46,559
it broke my heart even more.

660
00:28:46,839 --> 00:28:47,519
I just feel like...

661
00:28:47,799 --> 00:28:48,559
I did something wrong,

662
00:28:48,559 --> 00:28:50,400
but I don't even know what it was.

663
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,920
I feel like I failed to fulfill

664
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:54,000
my duty as a daughter-in-law.

665
00:28:54,079 --> 00:28:54,480
No, that's not it—

666
00:28:54,559 --> 00:28:56,079
I've made you suffer.

667
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,079
I feel like I can never make it up to you, Dad!

668
00:28:58,079 --> 00:28:58,759
No, Zhenzhu's mom...

669
00:28:59,119 --> 00:29:01,279
How can I ever make it right?

670
00:29:01,279 --> 00:29:02,880
That's not what I mean.

671
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:04,960
Look, I just wanted to make it up to—

672
00:29:06,279 --> 00:29:06,920
Zhenzhu's mom...

673
00:29:07,319 --> 00:29:08,759
That's really not what I meant. Please...

674
00:29:26,519 --> 00:29:27,880
Still upset, aren't you?

675
00:29:29,519 --> 00:29:31,480
Dad didn't really say anything against you, did he?

676
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:32,880
Even if he did,

677
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:35,200
that was all before we got married.

678
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:36,559
Besides,

679
00:29:37,039 --> 00:29:38,039
you haven't done anything

680
00:29:38,319 --> 00:29:39,519
to let the Sai family down.

681
00:29:39,839 --> 00:29:40,279
Third Brother,

682
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:41,160
Fourth Brother,

683
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,160
and Little Five—

684
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:43,480
didn't you raise all of them?

685
00:29:44,039 --> 00:29:44,359
And another thing,

686
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:45,920
when Stepmom was sick,

687
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:48,079
you were bustling about, tending to everything.

688
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:49,880
Dad saw all of that,

689
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:50,880
and he took it to heart.

690
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:54,119
You aren't worried the villagers

691
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,119
will gossip,

692
00:29:55,319 --> 00:29:56,839
saying you aren't filial to the old man?

693
00:29:57,039 --> 00:29:57,799
Don't worry.

694
00:29:57,799 --> 00:29:59,079
That'll never happen.

695
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:01,759
You're the saintly martyr of Qingyangli!

696
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:03,440
You don't know shit, Sai Xiuming!

697
00:30:05,279 --> 00:30:06,599
You think I actually care

698
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:08,480
what Dad and the neighbors think of me?

699
00:30:09,319 --> 00:30:10,039
If they praise me,

700
00:30:10,039 --> 00:30:11,079
does it put meat on my bones?

701
00:30:12,799 --> 00:30:14,240
Dad is playing us!

702
00:30:14,799 --> 00:30:16,359
He says he'll buy us an apartment,

703
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:18,039
but in whose name?

704
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,839
Whose name goes on the deed?

705
00:30:20,279 --> 00:30:21,720
He claims he's moving in with Second Brother,

706
00:30:22,079 --> 00:30:24,000
who hasn't lived at home in over ten years!

707
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:26,400
Can Second Brother and his wife really put up with him?

708
00:30:26,559 --> 00:30:27,880
Dad has his mind set

709
00:30:28,079 --> 00:30:30,640
on taking the construction team and money to him!

710
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:33,400
All these years,

711
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:35,720
humbling myself and slaving away like a mule,

712
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,400
waiting on all these people,

713
00:30:38,799 --> 00:30:39,839
I've done everything I was supposed to,

714
00:30:40,759 --> 00:30:42,319
endured all the dirty looks,

715
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:43,680
and in the end,

716
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,599
I get nothing at all!

717
00:30:46,279 --> 00:30:49,119
Look at the measly bit of cash on the table!

718
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:55,559
H-How about you...

719
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:56,240
You...

720
00:30:57,240 --> 00:30:57,759
Where are you going?

721
00:30:57,759 --> 00:30:58,240
To do something big.

722
00:31:02,279 --> 00:31:03,960
You need to talk sense into your genius brother.

723
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:06,160
Studying won't bring in cash like demolition!

724
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:06,519
Right?

725
00:31:06,599 --> 00:31:08,039
I told you not to touch Little Five's stuff!

726
00:31:09,119 --> 00:31:09,759
My place gets torn down,

727
00:31:09,839 --> 00:31:10,480
your place gets torn down...

728
00:31:10,839 --> 00:31:11,400
Does that make you rich,

729
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,079
or me?

730
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:13,279
When I get rich,

731
00:31:13,599 --> 00:31:14,319
you can be my lackey.

732
00:31:14,519 --> 00:31:15,400
Bro, I can be that right now!

733
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:17,000
Bro!

734
00:31:17,279 --> 00:31:17,839
Stop messing around.

735
00:31:18,079 --> 00:31:18,400
Bro!

736
00:31:19,279 --> 00:31:20,240
No, no, wait a second!

737
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:29,400
What do you want?

738
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:30,079
Let's talk.

739
00:31:30,519 --> 00:31:31,160
Talk about what?

740
00:31:31,519 --> 00:31:31,920
Dividing the estate.

741
00:31:36,079 --> 00:31:36,440
Get lost.

742
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:37,119
Wait, hold on...

743
00:31:37,359 --> 00:31:38,839
Let me listen. We're all family here.

744
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,119
Is your last name Sai?

745
00:31:40,519 --> 00:31:40,920
Whether my name is Sai or not—

746
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:41,319
Get lost!

747
00:31:41,359 --> 00:31:42,279
I've got experience, Big Brother.

748
00:31:42,279 --> 00:31:42,559
You...

749
00:31:42,559 --> 00:31:42,960
Get out.

750
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:44,039
Out, get out!

751
00:31:44,039 --> 00:31:44,400
I...

752
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:49,559
I tried talking to you so many times,

753
00:31:49,559 --> 00:31:50,160
and you never said a word.

754
00:31:50,480 --> 00:31:51,480
Why the change of heart today?

755
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,720
Dad's buying a place to live with the second brother.

756
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:54,559
What?

757
00:31:54,839 --> 00:31:56,599
Anyway, Dad made it clear to us today.

758
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:57,559
He's living with the second brother.

759
00:31:57,880 --> 00:31:59,079
For you and Eldest Brother,

760
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,200
he'll buy an apartment for each of you,

761
00:32:01,279 --> 00:32:02,480
and set aside some tuition for Xiao Wu.

762
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:03,279
Since that's how it is,

763
00:32:05,279 --> 00:32:06,319
what do I have left to look forward to?

764
00:32:06,519 --> 00:32:07,799
Wait, what's the old man thinking?

765
00:32:07,799 --> 00:32:09,039
How can he divide it like that?

766
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:10,920
Xiuhe.

767
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:14,640
I see things clearly now.

768
00:32:14,839 --> 00:32:16,160
You're an open scoundrel,

769
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:17,279
Watch your mouth!

770
00:32:17,279 --> 00:32:18,799
and they're hypocrites.

771
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:21,079
Doesn't Sai Xiuliang want the money?

772
00:32:21,759 --> 00:32:22,559
He's running all over the place,

773
00:32:22,559 --> 00:32:23,920
trying to get more compensation for our family.

774
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:24,440
Why?

775
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:26,000
Doesn't he just want a bigger cut?

776
00:32:26,079 --> 00:32:26,640
On Mid-Autumn Festival,

777
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,000
everyone will be there.

778
00:32:29,319 --> 00:32:30,319
I'll take the lead, you back me up.

779
00:32:30,559 --> 00:32:31,559
We'll lay it all out on the table.

780
00:32:31,759 --> 00:32:32,400
How about it?

781
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,480
Come, sit down.

782
00:32:45,759 --> 00:32:46,319
Don't you think

783
00:32:47,319 --> 00:32:47,799
we should first

784
00:32:48,599 --> 00:32:50,480
figure out how to split the money?

785
00:32:51,279 --> 00:32:52,440
Last time I invited you out to eat,

786
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,279
you wouldn't go.

787
00:32:53,920 --> 00:32:54,759
I've already figured it out.

788
00:32:55,119 --> 00:32:55,680
40, 30, 30.

789
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:57,079
Split between three families.

790
00:32:57,559 --> 00:32:58,640
Your family, Number Two's family,

791
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,240
plus me.

792
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:00,440
Whichever family the old man stays with

793
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:01,319
takes 40 percent.

794
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:02,240
That's the plan.

795
00:33:02,799 --> 00:33:03,920
What about Number Four and Number Five?

796
00:33:04,519 --> 00:33:05,359
Why count them?

797
00:33:05,680 --> 00:33:06,480
I'll handle Four and Five.

798
00:33:07,079 --> 00:33:07,839
You just focus on Number Two.

799
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,400
Four isn't short on cash anyway,

800
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,079
so count him out.

801
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,279
That won't work for Number Five.

802
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,400
Even if Five was adopted,

803
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,319
I'm still the one who raised him.

804
00:33:13,839 --> 00:33:14,839
The government made it official.

805
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,440
His surname is Sai. He's part of the family.

806
00:33:16,559 --> 00:33:17,160
The government stamped it?

807
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:17,920
Blood is what counts.

808
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:19,279
Just being raised by the Sais gets him a cut?

809
00:33:22,359 --> 00:33:25,000
You just want to lump Five under you

810
00:33:25,279 --> 00:33:26,240
to take an extra cut.

811
00:33:28,279 --> 00:33:28,920
Sai Xiuhe.

812
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,720
This is what Sai Xiuli deserves.

813
00:33:35,119 --> 00:33:35,640
Fine.

814
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,200
Then lay it on the table.

815
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:40,200
How should we split it?

816
00:33:40,559 --> 00:33:41,480
Our family of three,

817
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:43,359
plus Number Five.

818
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:44,720
We want this much.

819
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:45,759
As for the other half,

820
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:46,920
Dad can give it to whoever he likes.

821
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:47,839
How much?

822
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:49,319
That much? Are you insane?

823
00:33:49,519 --> 00:33:50,799
Dad will most likely live with Number Two.

824
00:33:50,799 --> 00:33:52,640
He'll want at least 40 percent.

825
00:33:52,720 --> 00:33:53,359
How much does that leave me?

826
00:33:53,359 --> 00:33:54,079
Ten percent.

827
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:54,920
What were you thinking?

828
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:55,400
I don't care.

829
00:33:56,079 --> 00:33:57,079
Either way, my family wants this much.

830
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:58,880
Worst case, Dad can live with us.

831
00:33:59,319 --> 00:33:59,920
Wen Jiayin.

832
00:34:00,839 --> 00:34:01,680
Aren't you something?

833
00:34:02,119 --> 00:34:03,920
Just by flapping your gums,

834
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,240
you're walking away with half.

835
00:34:05,599 --> 00:34:06,720
I took the lead back at Mid-Autumn,

836
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:07,720
and didn't even ask for the lion's share.

837
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:08,639
Yet here you are, stabbing me in the back.

838
00:34:08,639 --> 00:34:09,440
Me, stabbing you in the back?

839
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:11,480
Sai Xiuhe.

840
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,280
Search your conscience before you talk.

841
00:34:13,440 --> 00:34:14,960
If not for me and your eldest brother

842
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:15,719
holding things together inside and out,

843
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:16,519
this family would've fallen apart long ago.

844
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:17,800
Taking half?

845
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:19,599
This isn't robbery.

846
00:34:20,639 --> 00:34:22,199
After all our hard work over the past decade,

847
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:23,519
this is what we rightfully earned.

848
00:34:23,519 --> 00:34:24,360
Don't give me that crap.

849
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:25,280
I'm not buying it.

850
00:34:25,719 --> 00:34:26,440
30 percent.

851
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:27,199
That's my bottom line.

852
00:34:27,719 --> 00:34:28,320
Third Brother.

853
00:34:28,880 --> 00:34:31,199
You think making a scene like this

854
00:34:31,199 --> 00:34:32,320
will make Dad give you money?

855
00:34:32,599 --> 00:34:33,559
I'll tell you what'll happen:

856
00:34:33,559 --> 00:34:34,679
Dad will take the money and live with Number Two.

857
00:34:35,119 --> 00:34:36,239
You won't get a damn thing.

858
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:37,360
Not even a single dime.

859
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,239
I won't even get a dime?

860
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:39,159
You dare bring up Number Two?

861
00:34:39,239 --> 00:34:39,840
Let me tell you something.

862
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:40,360
If you push me too far,

863
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:41,280
I'll expose that Number Two quit his job.

864
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,079
I'll spill it all out.

865
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:43,719
Let's see who gets any money then!

866
00:34:54,679 --> 00:34:55,320
Well?

867
00:34:56,119 --> 00:34:56,880
Didn't see that coming, did you?

868
00:34:57,480 --> 00:34:58,039
Let me tell you,

869
00:34:58,519 --> 00:34:59,639
if I get shortchanged on my share,

870
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:01,320
even if Dad tears into me,

871
00:35:01,519 --> 00:35:02,920
I'll still light the fuse on this whole thing.

872
00:35:03,159 --> 00:35:04,320
Nobody will get a single cent!

873
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,960
The... the second brother quit his job.

874
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:11,679
Gave up his government post.

875
00:35:12,159 --> 00:35:13,320
Opened his own law firm.

876
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:14,679
He's living the high life now.

877
00:35:15,159 --> 00:35:15,800
How do you know?

878
00:35:17,159 --> 00:35:18,079
He mentioned it when buying his house.

879
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:19,079
It slipped out.

880
00:35:21,599 --> 00:35:22,920
Would Dad ever allow that?

881
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,280
Does Dad even know?

882
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:25,639
Who'd dare tell him?

883
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:26,320
Would you?

884
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:27,960
I sure wouldn't.

885
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:28,800
Let me tell you,

886
00:35:28,920 --> 00:35:30,559
if the old man finds out he quit his post,

887
00:35:30,679 --> 00:35:31,639
he'll lose all hope.

888
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:32,960
And once he loses hope,

889
00:35:33,039 --> 00:35:34,639
he'll clutch that money with an iron grip.

890
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:35,199
Divide it?

891
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:35,840
Divide what?

892
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:37,519
Then he'll turn around and think,

893
00:35:37,679 --> 00:35:39,039
"Third Brother, what were you thinking?

894
00:35:39,239 --> 00:35:40,519
You kept this from me.

895
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:42,719
Are you trying to stab your brother in the back?"

896
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:44,559
Don't walk away!

897
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,840
Think about that split.

898
00:35:45,840 --> 00:35:46,559
We can work something out!

899
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:17,360
Done with your big business?

900
00:36:18,440 --> 00:36:19,480
Now you can wash up and hit the sack.

901
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:04,519
Why is that new car parked downstairs?

902
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:06,519
Did your dad come over?

903
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,679
What's wrong? Why are you crying?

904
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:13,639
Well...

905
00:37:14,079 --> 00:37:14,559
My dad...

906
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:17,440
Cancer.

907
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:18,719
Pros... prostate cancer.

908
00:37:19,559 --> 00:37:21,440
The MRI basically confirmed it.

909
00:37:21,960 --> 00:37:22,519
Right now,

910
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:24,480
we're waiting on the biopsy results.

911
00:37:26,079 --> 00:37:26,320
Wait,

912
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,039
how did this happen?

913
00:37:28,519 --> 00:37:29,239
Who knows?

914
00:37:30,519 --> 00:37:31,679
When did this happen?

915
00:37:32,280 --> 00:37:32,880
I just found out.

916
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Honestly, growing up,

917
00:37:39,199 --> 00:37:40,519
it never even crossed my mind

918
00:37:41,519 --> 00:37:42,360
that my dad would get old.

919
00:37:44,079 --> 00:37:45,480
I never thought he'd get sick, either.

920
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:49,599
How could it suddenly be something so serious?

921
00:37:52,239 --> 00:37:53,440
Sure, he's a little heavy,

922
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:57,239
but he still acts like a young man.

923
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:00,280
He goes to the construction site every day.

924
00:38:02,039 --> 00:38:03,360
He has the loudest voice in the house,

925
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:06,000
and he eats the most.

926
00:38:09,519 --> 00:38:09,960
How could he...

927
00:38:11,599 --> 00:38:13,320
Look, the biopsy results aren't even out yet.

928
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:15,320
Even if it really turns out to be malignant,

929
00:38:15,599 --> 00:38:16,880
it's not the end of the world.

930
00:38:17,199 --> 00:38:18,280
We'll just get him the treatment he needs.

931
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:20,119
Besides, we have Jin Jingran at the hospital.

932
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:21,639
If they can't treat it in Honggang,

933
00:38:21,639 --> 00:38:22,679
we'll go to Shanghai or Beijing.

934
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:23,679
He'll definitely be cured.

935
00:38:24,519 --> 00:38:25,599
We'll take it one step at a time.

936
00:38:26,480 --> 00:38:27,159
I'll be right here with you.

937
00:38:48,199 --> 00:38:48,519
We're here.

938
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:49,599
Come with me to Second Yang's.

939
00:38:50,079 --> 00:38:50,480
What for?

940
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:51,800
You'll see when we get there.

941
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,800
What shady scheme are you hatching?

942
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:54,000
Second Uncle!

943
00:38:56,039 --> 00:38:56,519
Second Uncle!

944
00:38:57,840 --> 00:38:58,679
Look who's here, both of you.

945
00:38:58,679 --> 00:38:59,239
Keeping busy?

946
00:38:59,719 --> 00:39:00,239
Looking to buy something?

947
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:01,639
What are you looking to buy?

948
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:03,559
Always joking around with me.

949
00:39:05,159 --> 00:39:06,159
What is it you want to buy?

950
00:39:07,199 --> 00:39:08,039
I wanted to ask you...

951
00:39:08,039 --> 00:39:10,239
Have you been looking to buy anything, Second Uncle?

952
00:39:19,840 --> 00:39:20,599
Your brother didn't come?

953
00:39:21,159 --> 00:39:21,599
Second Uncle.

954
00:39:22,400 --> 00:39:23,559
That deal you discussed with my brother,

955
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:25,199
to buy out our construction crew...

956
00:39:26,159 --> 00:39:27,400
Think about how much equipment we have.

957
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:29,199
Does he know what any of it costs?

958
00:39:29,440 --> 00:39:30,639
Nearly 80 workers.

959
00:39:30,719 --> 00:39:31,840
Does he have any clue what they're worth?

960
00:39:32,079 --> 00:39:33,199
And just dumping the whole lot,

961
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:34,400
selling it off dirt cheap...

962
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,400
Selling off the family silver without a second thought.

963
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:37,119
All right, that's enough.

964
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:38,239
Lao San.

965
00:39:38,559 --> 00:39:39,519
Everything going on with your family,

966
00:39:39,519 --> 00:39:40,280
who doesn't know about it?

967
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:41,760
You think I'm an idiot?

968
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:42,280
Step aside.

969
00:39:43,519 --> 00:39:44,199
That job site...

970
00:39:45,159 --> 00:39:47,000
your tower crane is too rusted to even move.

971
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,119
The tracks won't even turn.

972
00:39:48,639 --> 00:39:50,199
Plenty of workers, sure—70 or 80 of them.

973
00:39:50,599 --> 00:39:52,119
Over half of them are past 50.

974
00:39:52,519 --> 00:39:54,239
I'm only doing this out of respect for your dad.

975
00:39:54,239 --> 00:39:55,119
I feel bad for him.

976
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:56,079
Otherwise,

977
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:57,280
I wouldn't touch this mess.

978
00:39:57,639 --> 00:39:58,920
Second Uncle, Second Uncle, hear me out.

979
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:00,719
As for our crew's projects,

980
00:40:00,719 --> 00:40:01,360
right now,

981
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:03,400
two are active, and three are in talks.

982
00:40:03,559 --> 00:40:04,079
And me,

983
00:40:04,079 --> 00:40:04,679
I ran the numbers.

984
00:40:04,880 --> 00:40:06,119
Break even in one year, double in two.

985
00:40:06,440 --> 00:40:07,840
You're an old pro, right?

986
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:08,800
Your math...

987
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:09,719
is sharper than mine.

988
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:10,400
I won't push you.

989
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:11,559
Think it over yourself.

990
00:40:12,239 --> 00:40:12,920
But when it comes to your family,

991
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:13,639
can you really call the shots?

992
00:40:13,719 --> 00:40:14,159
Either way,

993
00:40:14,159 --> 00:40:15,800
right now, my dad's ID card,

994
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,440
the ledgers, the official seal,

995
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:18,320
the business license...

996
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:19,320
I know where every last one is.

997
00:40:19,599 --> 00:40:20,719
Does Ma Laiqi know?

998
00:40:21,159 --> 00:40:22,239
That, I couldn't say for sure.

999
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:23,400
All right.

1000
00:40:23,760 --> 00:40:24,880
You're all from the Ma family,

1001
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:26,679
so I won't keep you in the dark.

1002
00:40:27,719 --> 00:40:28,519
What I offered your brother...

1003
00:40:28,519 --> 00:40:30,079
14,500.

1004
00:40:30,079 --> 00:40:30,679
That's the exact figure.

1005
00:40:30,679 --> 00:40:31,159
Cleared.

1006
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,880
1,550,000.

1007
00:40:46,559 --> 00:40:47,039
Clear.

1008
00:40:50,239 --> 00:40:50,559
One...

1009
00:40:52,239 --> 00:40:52,599
Lao San,

1010
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:55,239
this is my final offer.

1011
00:40:55,559 --> 00:40:56,079
...six, five...

1012
00:40:56,079 --> 00:40:56,920
Take it or leave it. ...zero, zero, zero, zero.

1013
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:57,280
If not,

1014
00:40:57,920 --> 00:40:58,360
no deal.

1015
00:40:59,199 --> 00:41:00,880
You're treating me like a beggar, huh?

1016
00:41:01,119 --> 00:41:01,800
What beggar?

1017
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:03,280
Where does a beggar ever get a handout this big?

1018
00:41:03,639 --> 00:41:04,079
Clear.

1019
00:41:04,639 --> 00:41:04,960
Two...

1020
00:41:05,559 --> 00:41:07,000
...zero, zero, zero, zero, zero, zero.

1021
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:07,599
Let's round it up.

1022
00:41:08,440 --> 00:41:08,719
Get out!

1023
00:41:10,199 --> 00:41:11,199
Why come here just to mess with me?

1024
00:41:11,199 --> 00:41:11,559
Out!

1025
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:12,360
All of you, get the hell out!

1026
00:41:13,119 --> 00:41:13,519
Big Bro...

1027
00:41:14,599 --> 00:41:16,199
Let's bounce. He's done talking.

1028
00:41:16,519 --> 00:41:17,039
Ma Laosan,

1029
00:41:17,719 --> 00:41:19,360
how do I always teach you to do business?

1030
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:21,840
It's a two-million deal, and you won't let him haggle?

1031
00:41:22,199 --> 00:41:23,760
Uncle isn't hurting for one or two hundred grand.

1032
00:41:24,159 --> 00:41:25,760
You've got to give Uncle a proper pitch.

1033
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:26,920
Service with a smile.

1034
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:27,800
Talk to him nicely.

1035
00:41:31,559 --> 00:41:32,880
Uncle, let me put it this way.

1036
00:41:33,119 --> 00:41:34,559
My dad is just sick.

1037
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:36,280
He's not dead.

1038
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,159
Say he recovers in a couple of days...

1039
00:41:38,559 --> 00:41:39,320
For two million,

1040
00:41:39,719 --> 00:41:40,480
would he sell to you?

1041
00:41:40,719 --> 00:41:41,519
Forget two million—

1042
00:41:41,679 --> 00:41:42,679
add another million, make it three—

1043
00:41:43,159 --> 00:41:43,920
do you think he'd sell to you?

1044
00:41:44,559 --> 00:41:45,880
Real estate is booming right now.

1045
00:41:46,079 --> 00:41:46,760
Everyone knows

1046
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:48,239
whoever has a construction crew rakes it in.

1047
00:41:48,480 --> 00:41:49,119
Miss this chance,

1048
00:41:49,159 --> 00:41:49,960
and you won't get another.

1049
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,000
Put it in writing.

1050
00:41:57,920 --> 00:41:58,519
Malay fabric.

1051
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:00,840
Auntie!

1052
00:42:01,079 --> 00:42:01,400
Get the hell out here!

1053
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:01,840
I'm talking business!

1054
00:42:02,079 --> 00:42:02,800
I'm talking business!

1055
00:42:02,920 --> 00:42:03,239
Wait--

1056
00:42:03,239 --> 00:42:04,639
Who gave you the nerve to sell the team?!

1057
00:42:04,639 --> 00:42:05,760
Auntie, I'm talking business here!

1058
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:06,840
We'll talk when we get home.

1059
00:42:07,679 --> 00:42:07,920
Wait, hold on--

1060
00:42:08,039 --> 00:42:08,440
Get moving, now!

1061
00:42:09,199 --> 00:42:10,280
I need to talk to you. Let's go!

1062
00:42:10,599 --> 00:42:11,000
Auntie!

1063
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,639
We have to sell the team right now!

1064
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:13,360
Venetian plaster.

1065
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:14,760
You're saying he and Yang Er...

1066
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:15,519
settled on 1.2 million?

1067
00:42:15,679 --> 00:42:16,320
How much did I get?

1068
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:17,280
Two million.

1069
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:18,119
Listen to you...

1070
00:42:19,400 --> 00:42:20,280
Why are you heading over here?

1071
00:42:20,840 --> 00:42:21,519
What's it to you?

1072
00:42:21,519 --> 00:42:22,039
Who are you?

1073
00:42:22,119 --> 00:42:22,960
What do you mean, "what's it to me"?

1074
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:23,639
This is my house!

1075
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:24,880
Is Sai Duoxi home?

1076
00:42:25,199 --> 00:42:25,800
I need to see him.

1077
00:42:26,320 --> 00:42:26,840
Old man!

1078
00:42:27,559 --> 00:42:28,239
You home?

1079
00:42:28,599 --> 00:42:29,039
Old man!

1080
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,639
A real beauty came all the way to see you!

1081
00:42:31,639 --> 00:42:32,079
Brother Duoxi!

1082
00:42:32,079 --> 00:42:32,760
Nonsense!

1083
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:33,079
Seriously!

1084
00:42:33,079 --> 00:42:33,440
Uncle!

1085
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:34,400
Who is it?

1086
00:42:34,840 --> 00:42:35,480
It's me.

1087
00:42:36,119 --> 00:42:37,239
Hao Zhihua.

1088
00:42:38,559 --> 00:42:39,400
You're...

1089
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:40,599
Ma Jiucheng is my brother-in-law.

1090
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:41,800
Guifen is my sister.

1091
00:42:42,119 --> 00:42:44,239
He brought me over to your place for dinner once.

1092
00:42:44,239 --> 00:42:45,679
That braised pork shank your wife made...

1093
00:42:45,679 --> 00:42:46,679
I ate three of them.

1094
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:47,800
You sat across from me and said,

1095
00:42:47,800 --> 00:42:49,280
"Careful, or you'll turn into a chubby girl,

1096
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:49,960
and no one will marry you."

1097
00:42:49,960 --> 00:42:51,239
I burst out crying right then and there!

1098
00:42:51,800 --> 00:42:52,440
Now that you mention it...

1099
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:53,079
I remember now.

1100
00:42:53,079 --> 00:42:53,760
I remember!

1101
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:55,000
The one who works at the bank!

1102
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:55,639
Yes, exactly!

1103
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:56,480
What brings you here?

1104
00:42:56,599 --> 00:42:57,159
Come on, have a seat inside.

1105
00:42:57,159 --> 00:42:58,119
I won't come in.

1106
00:42:58,880 --> 00:42:59,920
The reason I came today...

1107
00:43:00,199 --> 00:43:02,519
is to ask you to judge who's right.

1108
00:43:02,719 --> 00:43:03,519
It's about my eldest nephew.

1109
00:43:04,559 --> 00:43:05,679
On my way here just now,

1110
00:43:05,679 --> 00:43:06,760
he was at Yang Er's shop,

1111
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:08,000
trying to sell off our construction team!

1112
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:08,599
That's right, old man!

1113
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:09,440
I can vouch for that.

1114
00:43:09,639 --> 00:43:10,199
Selling it right in front of me!

1115
00:43:10,400 --> 00:43:11,119
Yang Er made an offer...

1116
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:22,039
I want to talk to you

1117
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:24,000
about the family assets.

1118
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:25,280
The only ones who get a cut in this family

1119
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:27,119
are the eldest, the second, and me.

1120
00:43:27,119 --> 00:43:28,000
Listen to yourself!

1121
00:43:28,039 --> 00:43:29,199
Do you think Dad's better off at your place,

1122
00:43:29,199 --> 00:43:29,880
or living with us?

1123
00:43:29,880 --> 00:43:30,840
Sister-in-law, I think you're being

1124
00:43:30,840 --> 00:43:32,079
a bit relentless with this.

1125
00:43:32,119 --> 00:43:33,039
But have you ever thought about it?

1126
00:43:33,039 --> 00:43:34,360
You just started a new company,

1127
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:36,159
and it's not even up and running yet.

1128
00:43:36,199 --> 00:43:37,840
If you run it while looking after Dad,

